{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "name": "outdoor_enclosure_pilot",
  "provenance": "Outdoor wall/pole-mounted electronics enclosure, pilot 50 units. Synthetic enclosure_fixture geometry (not a validated product design). Requirements, not physics: order quantity 50 and a 10 K margin between the housing maximum temperature and the conservative route-material service limit. Chain: spreadsheet variant -> conformal general-solid mesh -> steady enclosure conduction (docs/enclosure-thermal.md). Electronics power, site ambient, film and internal coefficients, solar load and board conductivity are declared inputs that stay missing until measured or specified, so the thermal child is refused (blocked) and the constraint stays unknown; nothing is defaulted. The pc-uv window has no sourced solar absorptance, so the solar-loaded solve is refused until one is sourced; PA12 routes are refused for the same reason. Replace source_job with an authorized enclosure_fixture job.",
